{"id": "EUVD-2026-98671", "enisaUuid": "abcc4a94-a853-375c-bd64-95878fbf2ea6", "description": "Wazuh from 4.1.1 before 4.14.8 contains a path traversal vulnerability in the get_lists() and delete_list_file() CDB list handlers that allows compromised cluster workers to read or delete master files. Attackers can send traversal or absolute-path filenames through the internal cluster RPC path, bypassing REST validation and RBAC to delete files like rbac.db.", "datePublished": "2026-10-13T13:27:27", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T21:52:27", "baseScore": 8.4, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:A/AC:L/AT:N/PR:H/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/wazuh/wazuh/security/advisories/GHSA-vc33-wcqf-cwgv", "https://github.com/wazuh/wazuh/releases/tag/v4.14.8", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/wazuh-from-4.1.1-before-4.14.8-path-traversal-in-cdb-list-cluster-handlers"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-74033"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.23, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "afa95ada-796f-39aa-a39c-22a0a78376b9", "product": {"name": "wazuh-manager", "vendor": {"name": "wazuh"}}, "product_version": "4.1.1 <4.14.8"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "6caf5c56-df68-394b-b674-463c0c65d3c2", "vendor": {"name": "wazuh"}}], "isExploited": false}